# Agent Workflow Rules

## Before starting any task

1. Read `docs/demo-tasks.md` to understand the full task description, steps, and acceptance criteria.
2. Run `npm run dev` in the background if you need to verify UI behavior.
3. Run `npm run db:reset` if the database state looks inconsistent.

## While implementing

- Work in small, focused commits. One logical change per commit.
- Add `data-testid` attributes to any new interactive elements you create.
- Do not modify `prisma/schema.prisma` unless the task explicitly requires it.
- Do not change existing `data-testid` values — tests depend on them.
- Do not install new dependencies without justification in the PR description.

## Before finishing — mandatory checklist

Run these commands in order and fix any errors before opening a PR:

```bash
npm run lint
npm run test
npm run test:e2e
```

All three must pass with zero errors. Do not open a PR if any of them fails.

## Opening the PR

Always open a pull request when the task is complete:

- **Title format:** `feat: <short description>` (or `fix:` / `chore:` as appropriate)
- **Base branch:** `main`
- **PR body must include:**
  - What was changed and why
  - Which acceptance criteria from `docs/demo-tasks.md` are now satisfied (checklist)
  - The output of `npm run test:e2e` (copy the summary line)
  - Screenshots or a brief description of the visual change if the task touches UI

## Database

- The SQLite database (`prisma/dev.db`) is local and not in the repo.
- To reset to the seeded state: `npm run db:reset`
- Demo credentials: `demo@example.com` / `demo1234`
- The app always runs on port **3000**.

## What NOT to do

- Do not commit `.env` or `prisma/dev.db`.
- Do not use `--no-verify` to skip git hooks.
- Do not push directly to `main` — always use a PR.
- Do not leave `console.log` statements in production code.
- Do not modify files outside the scope of the current task.
